# Claude Code session state (local only)
#
# These are per-session working documents, not publishable artifacts. The harness
# generates them in whatever project it runs in (the output path comes from
# CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR), so when the harness itself is the project under work they
# land here. What ships is the generator in hooks/, never the generated state.
#
# They live in .gitignore rather than .git/info/exclude on purpose: exclude is
# not committed, so it only ever protects the one machine it was written on. A
# fresh clone — or a second PC — would otherwise have nothing stopping
# `git add -A` from publishing a session plan or a private path.
.claude/state/
.claude/harness-answers.yml
session-dashboard.html
CURRENT_SESSION.md
SESSION_INDEX.md
WORK_PLAN.md
